seg-744e95749978 = A clock scenario may carry an <c1/> section (<c2/>): a site (<c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/>), constellation presets (<c6/>, default <c7/>), a mask, a range-residual sigma, the false-alarm and missed-detection probabilities, the horizontal and vertical alert limits, an epoch spacing and an optional stated bias on one satellite. The run then reports a separate <c8/> block: per epoch the satellites in view, the snapshot RAIM protection levels and a verdict (<c9/>, <c10/>, <c11/>, <c12/>, <c13/>), and the counts and availability over the run. While the timeline says GNSS is denied, RAIM is unavailable and nothing is extrapolated; a degraded window is evaluated as nominal. The holdover figures of merit are unchanged, and without the section the output is byte-identical. MODELLED: a representative preset sky, synthetic residuals and stated limits. It needs <c14/>.

